{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780417942,"nonce":"FHGY3Hz+ETQHEDoW7F1pFGVXgyA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEJXTSg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/206","origin":"github"},"title":"Enable controller-layer obstacle avoidance on BizzyBoat (nav2_overlay FollowPath flip)","message":"## Summary\n\nEnable controller-layer survey-line obstacle avoidance on BizzyBoat by flipping\nthe `FollowPath` controller plugin (in `bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`,\nBizzyBoat-only) from the bare `CrabbingPathFollower` to the new\n`marine_nav_avoidance_controller::AvoidanceController` decorator, with crabbing as\nits inner (`primary_controller`).\n\nThis is the deploy-side half of the obstacle-avoidance rearchitecture\n(rolker/unh_marine_navigation#59), which moves avoidance off the BT node and into\na controller decorator that reshapes the followed path against the\ncontroller_server's own in-process costmap.\n\n## ⚠️ Hard dependency / ordering\n\n**Do not merge or deploy this before\n[`marine_nav_avoidance_controller`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/60)\nis merged and `core_ws` is rebuilt on the boat.** Without the plugin installed,\n`controller_server` cannot load `AvoidanceController` and the boat will have no\n`FollowPath` controller. Deploy the two together.\n\n## Change\n\nAdd a `controller_server` section to `nav2_overlay.yaml` (deep-merged over\nseafloor's `nav2_params.base.yaml`):\n\n- `FollowPath.plugin` → `marine_nav_avoidance_controller::AvoidanceController`\n- `FollowPath.primary_controller` → `marine_nav_crabbing_path_follower::CrabbingPathFollower`\n- avoidance tunables (`obstacle_avoidance_weight: 1.0` for a visible bend,\n  `anchor_behind_distance`, etc.)\n\nThe inner crabbing keeps reading the base's `FollowPath.default_speed` / `pid.*` /\n`visualization` (same `FollowPath` param namespace), so the tracker is unchanged.\nOther EchoBoats (seafloor, ben) keep crabbing-direct — this is BizzyBoat-only.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Stack relaunches healthy; `controller_server` loads `AvoidanceController` (log line).\n- Sim: the ahead path re-plans against a live/clearing costmap; the boat actually\n  rounds a stationary obstacle (the rolker/unh_marine_navigation#57 symptom is gone).\n- Confirm the progress-checker doesn't abort during a large deviation.\n- On-water validation before the June 15 survey.\n\nPart of rolker/unh_marine_navigation#59. Activates the fix for rolker/unh_marine_navigation#57.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: ``\n**Model**: ``","files":null}]}